      "html": "<h3>What is an internal audit under ISO 9001, 14001 and 45001?</h3><p>A planned audit you do on yourself at set intervals. It checks that your management system meets the standard and your own procedures. You raise nonconformities where practice has drifted. Corrective action is taken and checked. The results go to management review. One audit can cover all three standards.</p><h3>Must internal auditors be independent of the area they audit?</h3><p>The standards ask for an objective and impartial programme. In practice, nobody audits their own work. Check the wording of your standard and your certification body's rules.</p><h3>How does an audit app help with corrective actions?</h3><p>The common fault is losing the finding before it is fixed. A good app records the nonconformity on the spot, gives the action an owner, and tracks it to closure on a dashboard. Quickler does this. It does not judge whether a finding is a nonconformity. You do.</p><h3>Can I run internal audits in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Each checklist item arrives in your WhatsApp chat. You answer by text, voice note or photo of the evidence. When you say done, Quickler writes the report.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/compliance-audit-software-uk.html\">Compliance audit software for multi-site organisations</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/permit-to-work-system-app-uk.html\">Permit to work system and audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/contractor-compliance-audit-uk.html\">Contractor compliance and induction audits</a></li></ul>"
